{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1295890-vulgarity-and-sanctum-are-some-effects-always-vulgar","id":1295890,"title":"Vulgarity and Sanctum; are some effects ALWAYS Vulgar?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-11T12:07:26-07:00","id":1295890,"title":"Vulgarity and Sanctum; are some effects ALWAYS Vulgar?","content":"So in M20 some effects are labeled Vulgar automatically. Certain Time and Prime effects for example; pulling Quintessence out of the universe itself is Vulgar Prime 5 magick.<br /> <br /> But part of the Sanctum background is this space where your work is always Coincidental, since you define reality. Which takes precedence? Also, do people know all of the effects that are always Vulgar? I know a few but I'm sure I've missed most of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T12:30:43-07:00","id":1295899,"title":"","content":"The short answer is, yes, they are still Vulgar in your Sanctum. Something that is always Vulgar is Vulgar despite local reality zones so is unaffected by your Sanctum.<br /> <br /> The longer answer is that when you dig into the always Vulgar spells there is usually a specific reason they have that status. Something about them is specifically rejected by some aspect of reality. For instance, in the case of Time Travel the Mage is creating a temporal paradox, which is not specifically the same thing as Paradox but it does violate expectations in a broadly similar way*. In some way the Paradox is coming from something other than the spell itself. <br /> <br /> *I'm actually against the idea of using Paradox as the method for dealing with temporal paradoxes, but it is the rule right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T12:57:03-07:00","id":1295910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1295890-vulgarity-and-sanctum-are-some-effects-always-vulgar?p=1295899#post1295899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The short answer is, yes, they are still Vulgar in your Sanctum. Something that is always Vulgar is Vulgar despite local reality zones so is unaffected by your Sanctum.<br /> <br /> The longer answer is that when you dig into the always Vulgar spells there is usually a specific reason they have that status. Something about them is specifically rejected by some aspect of reality. For instance, in the case of Time Travel the Mage is creating a temporal paradox, which is not specifically the same thing as Paradox but it does violate expectations in a broadly similar way*. In some way the Paradox is coming from something other than the spell itself.<br /> <br /> *I'm actually against the idea of using Paradox as the method for dealing with temporal paradoxes, but it is the rule right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you could say that these effects defy the Earthly Foundations. There's no reality zone that accepts such effects because it's inherent to reality that time moves forward and similar.<br /> <br /> The only other example I've found of &quot;always vulgar&quot; is the immediate healing of Aggravated damage, since you're reweaving parts of a pattern that have been destroyed. I imagine that simply speeding up the natural healing of Aggravated damage is Coincidental though, if done in the right way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 03-11-2019, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T13:05:06-07:00","id":1295914,"title":"","content":"Yes, there are effects that are Vulgar even in Sanctums. For instance:<br /> <br /> *Healing Aggravated wounds it's Always Vulgar.<br /> <br /> *Very Epic Stuff, like breaking the Curse of Caine and other &quot;imposibilities&quot; that may or may not go against the will of God are also signaled as Always Vulgar<br /> <br /> *Gilgul it's Always Vulgar<br /> <br /> However, the limits between Vulgar and Always Vulgar are very dubious and rely a lot on ST fiat. These are exceptions to the general rule (much like gaining extra Paradox point when using Time 3 to rewind time) and should be treated like that.<br /> <br /> The language itself can be misleading:<br /> <br /> Sometimes it's said that something it's always going to be Vulgar because it's nigh impossible to hidde as a Coincidence, like when more than 10 points of Quintessence are moved in one round and magick starts to spark. In these cases it's not going to be Vulgar within a Sanctum (unless you yourself have a strong disbelef in such displays)<br /> <br /> Other times it's always Vulgar because it breaks Earthly Foundations...which it's a Vulgarity that won't necessarily apply in the Other Worlds. For instance, temporal and spatial distortions are very common in the Umbra, and magick that aligns with these isn't going to be Vulgar. As a more specific example, the Vulgar+ effect of rewinding time with Time 3 can be Coincident in the Digital Web (i.e: restore a saved game)<br /> <br /> Another thing of interest it's what happens with Always Vulgar in the Deep Umbra - where you can't gain Paradox because it doesn't exist there (as per Infinite Tapestry). An argument can be made that the spell it's still casted at the difficulty of a Vulgar spell, but you don't gain any Paradox. However one could contest that w/o Paradox the difference of difficulty understood as the resistance of Reality to the change has no reason to be.<br /> <br /> So, sometimes Always Vulgar may as well mean &quot;Most Of The Time Vulgar&quot; , and the limits of such category are heavily dependant on the ST. But yes, Vulgarity that transcends Sanctums and perhaps even Realms it's very much contemplated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-11-2019, 04:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T22:12:00-07:00","id":1296041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1295890-vulgarity-and-sanctum-are-some-effects-always-vulgar?p=1295914#post1295914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Healing Aggravated wounds it's Always Vulgar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it depends on the nature of the aggravated damage.<br /> For example, I don't see how healing aggravated damage from acid or fire would be more or less vulgar inside your Sanctum or a fitting reality zone than any other damage would be.<br /> Aggravated Damage to your very soul or the very concept of your Life Pattern (think Heart's Blood, which can't even be healed magically, period) on the other hand...it's more a fundamental Metaphysical sort of damage that transcends paradigm. An &quot;Otherworldy Foundation&quot; if you will.<br /> <br /> As Aleph said, likewise both Gilgul and healing the Curse of Caine are concepts that transcend paradigm, and again violate a very sort of Earthly - or Metaphyiscal - foundation. It's essentially you violating a big Power That Be, hence always vulgar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T06:15:51-07:00","id":1296105,"title":"","content":"They had a very good explanation for this in Masters of the Art, fluff wise at least.<br /> <br /> Things that are always vulgar violate the consensus, and believability, on so many levels that it's more or less impossible to create a stable reality zone that can include it as part of default reality. You would be spreading the concept of reality so thin as to make a hole of pure chaos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T07:29:08-07:00","id":1296122,"title":"","content":"This isn't a good explanation because it clashes with the much more fundamental notion that stuff that exists outside human experience exists also outside the Consensus, being Coincident most of the time (hence why stuff like sensing souls or magick it's never Vulgar unless you alter the perception of Sleepers, or why moving Quintessence it's almost always Coincident unless you move big quantities).<br /> <br /> A lot of things that are Always Vulgar aren't really distingusihable from Coincident stuff by any human means: Gilgul does something to the Avatar that's completely outside human experience. Aggravated damage doesn't even exist unless you try to heal it with magick (w/o magick it heals the same as normal damage - woud you make it more Vulgar than healing evident Lethal damage if rules weren't very specific about that?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-12-2019, 10:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T07:59:27-07:00","id":1296136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1295890-vulgarity-and-sanctum-are-some-effects-always-vulgar?p=1296122#post1296122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't a good explanation because it clashes with the much more fundamental notion that stuff that exists outside human experience exists also outside the Consensus, being Coincident most of the time (hence why stuff like sensing souls or magick it's never Vulgar unless you alter the perception of Sleepers, or why moving Quintessence it's almost always Coincident unless you move big quantities).<br /> <br /> A lot of things that are Always Vulgar aren't really distingusihable from Coincident stuff by any human means: Gilgul does something to the Avatar that's completely outside human experience. Aggravated damage doesn't even exist unless you try to heal it with magick (w/o magick it heals the same as normal damage - woud you make it more Vulgar than healing evident Lethal damage if rules weren't very specific about that?)</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea that the Consensus is entirely determined by sleeper belief is wrong though. Erasing someone's Avatar is Vulgar because it goes so thoroughly against the grain with one of reality's central features. Same goes for restoring parts of a pattern that have been unwoven. Sleepers don't need to have strong opinions one way or another on certain things. For example, undoing the Curse of Caine wouldn't be Vulgar if Sleeper opinion was the only thing to consider. But it is Vulgar because you're working against the powers of a powerful god/spirit, or The One itself even. For similar reasons it would probably be automatically Vulgar if you tried to turn a Garou into a normal wolf or human, or tried to turn a normal wolf or human into a Garou.<br /> <br /> So when we get down to it, it seems that we have to worry about the Consensus, and the Earthly Foundations that lie under the Consensus. Sleeper opinion is not the be all and end all; it's just incredibly important in determining most features of a reality zone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T08:55:53-07:00","id":1296150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1295890-vulgarity-and-sanctum-are-some-effects-always-vulgar?p=1296136#post1296136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The idea that the Consensus is entirely determined by sleeper belief is wrong though. Erasing someone's Avatar is Vulgar because it goes so thoroughly against the grain with one of reality's central features. Same goes for restoring parts of a pattern that have been unwoven. Sleepers don't need to have strong opinions one way or another on certain things. For example, undoing the Curse of Caine wouldn't be Vulgar if Sleeper opinion was the only thing to consider. But it is Vulgar because you're working against the powers of a powerful god/spirit, or The One itself even. For similar reasons it would probably be automatically Vulgar if you tried to turn a Garou into a normal wolf or human, or tried to turn a normal wolf or human into a Garou.<br /> <br /> So when we get down to it, it seems that we have to worry about the Consensus, and the Earthly Foundations that lie under the Consensus. Sleeper opinion is not the be all and end all; it's just incredibly important in determining most features of a reality zone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. It's important to decouple Consensus, Reality and Paradox. These are very related but are different words for a reason.<br /> <br /> The Consensus it's determined by human belief. There's no question about that, that's why it's called &quot;<i>Consensus</i>&quot;. This is explicitly stated in ALL Mage books ever (even talking about unreliable narrators isn't helpful here because mages <i>invented </i>that term - they presumably know what they meant)<br /> <br /> BUT Reality (and Paradox, as the force that reacts to counter alterations to Reality) MAY not be entirely determined by it.<br /> <br /> The idea behind the Cosmological Constants that were introduced in Revised and latter traduced into (somewhat weaker) Eartly Foundations was that there were stuff that seemed to resist change regarldess of the local Consensus. It was thoerized that perhaps these came from forces transcending the Consensus itself (the Triat and God are mentioned in Revised). But it was also theorized that perhaps these were just things that were ingrained in the human subconscious and thus always present to some extent (Vampires exist becuase humans subconsciously know that they have to - bullshit, I know, but canon bullshit) but not inherently beyond the Consensus power to change<br /> <br /> For those that believe that the Consensus it's omnipotent or nearly so there's nothing that's Truly Always Vulgar. Even stuff like lifting the Curse of Caine may be made Coincident, eventually. For those that believe that there are cosmic laws precluding humanity the &quot;Always Vulgar&quot; category does represent a fundamental change of the universe that Reality resists at a fundamental level. But there's no doubt about what the Consensus *is*<br /> <br /> When I'm not agreeing with Enginseer-42 interpretation of MotA fluf, I'm not agreeing with the notion that believability has anything to do with it.<br /> <br /> MotA it's talking about Archspheres, btw, not about the Always Vulgar category. It's important to note that Archspheres AREN'T Always Vulgar (altrough their Vulgarity does transcend Sanctums). Archspheres are Vulgar on Earth, but can be Coincident within Realms attuned with the mage's Paradigm, as per MotA.<br /> <br /> In theory, regenerating Aggravated would be Vulgar even within the Umbra (perhaps even in the Deep, where Paradox does not exist).<br /> <br /> As you see, this IS a complex issue. As it often happens with exceptions to the normal rules","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-12-2019, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T09:17:45-07:00","id":1296160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1295890-vulgarity-and-sanctum-are-some-effects-always-vulgar?p=1296136#post1296136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The idea that the Consensus is entirely determined by sleeper belief is wrong though. Erasing someone's Avatar is Vulgar because it goes so thoroughly against the grain with one of reality's central features.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not wrong. It depends on how you want to approach the game. For instance, one of the theories of how the Consensus have power is that the sleeping Avatars of humanity are themselves forming reality. In that case, the Vulgarity could be based in the Avatar being destroyed or on an inherent rejection of all Avatars to one of their own being destroyed. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In a very Same goes for restoring parts of a pattern that have been unwoven. Sleepers don't need to have strong opinions one way or another on certain things. For example, undoing the Curse of Caine wouldn't be Vulgar if Sleeper opinion was the only thing to consider. But it is Vulgar because you're working against the powers of a powerful god/spirit, or The One itself even. For similar reasons it would probably be automatically Vulgar if you tried to turn a Garou into a normal wolf or human, or tried to turn a normal wolf or human into a Garou.<br /> <br /> So when we get down to it, it seems that we have to worry about the Consensus, and the Earthly Foundations that lie under the Consensus. Sleeper opinion is not the be all and end all; it's just incredibly important in determining most features of a reality zone. </div> </div> </div>For the record I am a strong proponent of not relying on the Earthly Foundations (or of just considering them part of reality that has a lot of inertia, which amounts to the same thing). In that spirit, I think you are assuming things you don't have to.<br /> <br /> For example, even if reality is determined by the consensus that doesn't mean it is fully determined by the consensus as it is now. For instance, it could build things up or erode them over time, such that the longer and stronger the belief in an idea the harder it is to erode away. So millennium of belief in an idea could build up something strongly enough that it acts like an immutable fact, but really there just hasn't been enough time to wear it away.<br /> <br /> It also isn't 100% necessary to limit the consensus to humans. Though later books have implied this was the case, 2nd edition clearly called out spirits as having an impact.<br /> <br /> I'm going to stop before I dive down a rabbit hole, though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T10:05:36-07:00","id":1296169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1295890-vulgarity-and-sanctum-are-some-effects-always-vulgar?p=1296160#post1296160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also isn't 100% necessary to limit the consensus to humans. Though later books have implied this was the case, 2nd edition clearly called out spirits as having an impact.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that is still true in M20, at least in regards to the Umbra...however I didn't wanted to enter there because that takes us to the &quot;reach&quot; of the Consensus...<br /> <br /> One <i>might </i>say that Vulgar it's a question of reach, explaining thus how it's that far away Realms laugh at things that elsewhere are regarded as &quot;reality's central features&quot; (Well, spirits have more sway here, humans have more sway there). But really that's a rabbit hole of it's own, and &quot;Always Vulgar&quot; is one of these dark aspects of the lore where the ST has to decide","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-12-2019, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T17:05:01-07:00","id":1296272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1295890-vulgarity-and-sanctum-are-some-effects-always-vulgar?p=1296136#post1296136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The idea that the Consensus is entirely determined by sleeper belief is wrong though. Erasing someone's Avatar is Vulgar because it goes so thoroughly against the grain with one of reality's central features. Same goes for restoring parts of a pattern that have been unwoven. Sleepers don't need to have strong opinions one way or another on certain things. For example, undoing the Curse of Caine wouldn't be Vulgar if Sleeper opinion was the only thing to consider. But it is Vulgar because you're working against the powers of a powerful god/spirit, or The One itself even. For similar reasons it would probably be automatically Vulgar if you tried to turn a Garou into a normal wolf or human, or tried to turn a normal wolf or human into a Garou.<br /> <br /> So when we get down to it, it seems that we have to worry about the Consensus, and the Earthly Foundations that lie under the Consensus. Sleeper opinion is not the be all and end all; it's just incredibly important in determining most features of a reality zone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Erasing someone's avatar is vulgar for the same reason unwilling human sacrifice doesn't work. In that moment, the victims Avatar is 100% focused on 'No this is wrong and can't happen.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T07:19:31-07:00","id":1296410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1295890-vulgarity-and-sanctum-are-some-effects-always-vulgar?p=1296272#post1296272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Erasing someone's avatar is vulgar for the same reason unwilling human sacrifice doesn't work. In that moment, the victims Avatar is 100% focused on 'No this is wrong and can't happen.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Unwilling numan sacrifice isn't particularly Vulgar, though. According to Revised it just taints the energy with antagonistic Ressonance preventing you from gaining power from the sacrifice.<br /> <br /> It's odd for a single Avatar to influence Paradox so much. The case I can think off it's, ironically, the creation of a Sanctum...but that takes time and effort, and this is SUPERSEDING that. Perhaps Avatars just pull that much harder when they're on the ropes. So I would say it <i>IS possible...</i><br /> <br /> ...but you're extrapolating a methaphisic to justify something that isn't really explained. I could do the same and say, like <i>Ramnesis </i>that if ALL Avatars inherently reject such feat then of course it's Vulgar...or like <i>11twiggins </i>grab upon the Cosmological Constants and say that Always Vulgar it's a consequence of cosmic law, hence Avatars aren't supposed to die. There's no reason to go either way, it's a personal choice <hr /><br /> On an unrelated note, while the language Revised employs in Prime 2 does suggest that such unwilling sacrifices are useless, there are rules for Quintessence with Ressonance diametrically opposed to your intent, and generally it's just a raise of the difficulty...that would defeat the purpose of burning it to lower diff, but doesn't sound nearly bad enough as to call it &quot;useless&quot;. So, either this effect uses a different rule for Ressonance that's never ever mentioned again...or it's uselessness it's greatly exaggerated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-13-2019, 10:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T16:53:43-07:00","id":1296825,"title":"","content":"M20 suggested that a spell that does something that the earthly foundations oppose can be coincidental, but only with great care taken to take them into account while still creating the effect. I think it said a person flying is always vulgar, but airplanes, thanks to the technocratic paradigm, are coincidental. So I imagine a hermetic working through the right steps could make something similar happen in a reality zone that accepts the hermetic paradigm. I'm not really sure what that would look like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":20546,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20546-dragonchild","user":"Dragonchild","date":". 03-14-2019, 07:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20546-dragonchild","name":"Dragonchild","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T12:06:47-07:00","id":1297054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonchild</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1295890-vulgarity-and-sanctum-are-some-effects-always-vulgar?p=1296825#post1296825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">M20 suggested that a spell that does something that the earthly foundations oppose can be coincidental, but only with great care taken to take them into account while still creating the effect. I think it said a person flying is always vulgar, but airplanes, thanks to the technocratic paradigm, are coincidental. So I imagine a hermetic working through the right steps could make something similar happen in a reality zone that accepts the hermetic paradigm. I'm not really sure what that would look like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, a buddhists monk that levitates in meditation comes to mind. That's a very established thing.<br /> <br /> Also Sanctums are, by their nature, places where great care has been taken to ingrain a sort of magick. All mages are expected to be able to do crazy stuff in their places.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}